<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Scaling Residual Stream Experiments</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">These models are all trained on Nvidia GeForce RTX 3090 gpus with a batch size of 64. All models use a max learning rate of <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1e^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1e^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math> and are trained over 50K steps. The models have 12 layers, residual matrix value dimension <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> of 64, 3072 feed-forward neurons, and a layer rank <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote8" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">8</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            Same <math id="footnote8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> from Eqs. in §<a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2 Residual Matrix Transformer ‣ 2 Model Architecture ‣ Residual Matrix Transformers: Scaling the Size of the Residual Stream" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a></span></span></span> of 12 for a total of 135M parameters. Note that <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to the number of attention heads, <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R*D_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R*D_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is input/output dimension of the core feed-forward operation (Eq. <a href="#S2.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ FeedForward Layer ‣ 2.2 Residual Matrix Transformer ‣ 2 Model Architecture ‣ Residual Matrix Transformers: Scaling the Size of the Residual Stream" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>), and <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is the attention head dimension.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Transformer Variants Experiments</h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All models were trained on Geforce-RTX 3090 gpus with a batch size a 64. They were trained for 5000 train steps for a total of 1.6B train tokens. The models all had 12 layers, <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{FF}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{FF}</annotation></semantics></math> of 3072, 12 attention heads, and <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> = 64. For the RMT model <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> was set to 32 and <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> was set to 64. Table <a href="#A3.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ C.4 Transformer Variants Experiments ‣ Appendix C Experimental Setup ‣ Residual Matrix Transformers: Scaling the Size of the Residual Stream" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> shows the models size and residual stream sizes for these models. The max learning rate was set to <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1e^{-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1e^{-2}</annotation></semantics></math> and we used Lecun initialization for all parameters.</p>
</div>
